{"builder":"Add a --shout flag to greet-cli in one pull request that meets these lines:\n1. node bin/greet.js --shout <name> prints the greeting in upper case\n2. without --shout the output is unchanged\n3. docs/index.md documents --shout\n4. after merge, the published docs page at https://o.github.io/greet-cli/ lists --shout\n\nSteps:\n- Read bin/greet.js, src/greet.js, test/greet.test.js, docs/index.md and .github/workflows/pages.yml.\n- In bin/greet.js, detect --shout among the arguments (in any position relative to the name). When it is present, write the greeting in upper case (e.g. `HELLO, ADA!`). The name must still be taken from the first argument that does not start with `--`, so `--shout` is never treated as the name. When --shout is absent, keep the output exactly as it is now (`Hello, <name>!` plus a newline), and keep the existing usage error when no name is given.\n- Keep greeting() in src/greet.js unchanged, or only add an optional behaviour that leaves greeting(name) returning the same result as now.\n- Add tests to test/greet.test.js: `node bin/greet.js --shout Ada` prints `HELLO, ADA!\\n`, `node bin/greet.js Ada --shout` gives the same, and the existing test for `node bin/greet.js Ada` printing `Hello, Ada!\\n` still passes.\n- Update docs/index.md to document --shout: show a usage line such as `node bin/greet.js --shout <name>` and say that it prints the greeting in upper case. Keep the existing content.\n- The published page is built from the docs folder by .github/workflows/pages.yml on pushes to main. Do not change that workflow; documenting --shout in docs/index.md is what makes the published page list it after merge.\n- Run `npm test` and make sure every test passes before you open the pull request.","verifier":"Run every check at the pull request's head. First run `npm test` once to get context; the checks below decide the result.\n\nCheck 1. Expect line: \"node bin/greet.js --shout <name> prints the greeting in upper case\"\nRun: `node bin/greet.js --shout Ada`.\nPASS: the output is the greeting in upper case, i.e. the normal greeting for Ada (`Hello, Ada!`) with every letter upper-cased (`HELLO, ADA!`).\nFAIL: the command errors, prints nothing, prints the greeting with any lower-case letters, or treats `--shout` as the name.\n\nCheck 2. Expect line: \"without --shout the output is unchanged\"\nRun: `node bin/greet.js Ada` at the head, and also at the base of the pull request (for example `git show <base>:bin/greet.js` into a temporary copy of the repo, or `git worktree add` at the merge base), then compare the two outputs. Also run `node bin/greet.js` with no arguments in both places.\nPASS: for both commands the output at the head is the same as at the base (`Hello, Ada!` for the first).\nFAIL: either output differs between head and base.\n\nCheck 3. Expect line: \"docs/index.md documents --shout\"\nRead docs/index.md at the head.\nPASS: the file mentions `--shout` and says what it does (makes the greeting upper case / louder).\nFAIL: the file does not mention `--shout`, or mentions it without saying what it does.\n\nCheck 4. Expect line: \"after merge, the published docs page at https://o.github.io/greet-cli/ lists --shout\"\nThe live page can only be seen after merge; do not fetch it. Instead read .github/workflows/pages.yml and docs/index.md at the head.\nPASS: the pages workflow still publishes the docs folder on pushes to main, and docs/index.md at the head lists `--shout`, so the published page will list it after merge.\nFAIL: the workflow no longer publishes docs (removed, trigger changed away from main, or path changed so docs/index.md is not published), or docs/index.md at the head does not list `--shout`.\n\nAdvisory (not part of PASS/FAIL):\n- `node bin/greet.js Ada --shout` should also print `HELLO, ADA!`.\n- `npm test` should exit 0, and the PR should add tests for --shout.\n- The exact expected shout output is `HELLO, ADA!` followed by a newline."}